<title>UK: LucasVarity up as share trading begins.</title>
<headline>LucasVarity up as share trading begins.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-09-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in auto components maker LucasVarity Plc rose on Friday at the start of trading in the newly merged Anglo-U.S. group.</p>
<p>The shares were up 8p at 239p at the beginning of trading at 1330 GMT. Varity Corp shares were simultaneously delisted from the S&amp;P 500 in the U.S.</p>
<p>LucasVarity is expected to be included in the FTSE 100 following the quarterly review of the index on September 11.</p>
<p>Lucas Industies Plc's  LUCS.L merger with Varity Corp was approved by both sets of shareholders in August.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 8712</p>
